<section class="ac-royal sunk section" style="padding-bottom: 80px;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Frequently Asked Questions</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Fashion and footwear questions, answered.</h2>
    </div>
    <div style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto;">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          How does Teamwork handle complex size/width/color matrices?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Teamwork's mobile native interface uses a high-density matrix view designed for footwear and apparel. Associates see stock levels across all sizes, widths, and colors in one screen, and can check availability at nearby stores instantly. If a size is out of stock, "Save the Sale" ships from another location in 3 taps.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          How does RFID help with mismatched pairs and missing inventory?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>RFID solves the mismatched-pair problem by tracking every individual unit. Associates use the RFID handheld's locate mode, which reads the tag's signal more strongly as they close in, to find the exact item in the backroom in seconds.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          How does Teamwork handle the high return rates in fashion?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Fashion has some of the highest online return rates in retail. Teamwork's BORIS (Buy Online Return In Store) processes cross-channel returns and restocks inventory the moment an item comes back, available for the next walk-in shopper right away, with no sync lag and no manual reconciliation.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          How does RFID self-checkout work for fashion retail?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Customers place items near the RFID antenna, the system detects every tagged item in seconds without barcode scanning or line-of-sight. Transactions complete in 30 seconds or less.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          How quickly can we deploy to new stores or markets?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Lammle's set up eleven pop-up stores at the Calgary Stampede in 10 days on Teamwork's mobile POS. The iOS interface reduces training to under 30 minutes. The platform is localized in 40+ countries with native fiscal compliance, so entering Paris, Sydney, or Mexico City requires no platform change, no regional vendor, and no re-training.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          How does this compare to other POS platforms for fashion retail?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Teamwork Commerce is the only one of the three with native RFID. Shopify POS is built for e-commerce first, so its in-store capabilities are secondary and it lacks native RFID; NewStore focuses on mobile-first associate experience but does not offer RFID self-checkout or RFID inventory. For a fashion retailer the deciding factor is usually inventory accuracy, since both markdowns and oversells trace back to it. Stock verified by <a href="/platform/rfid/" style="color: var(--brand-text);">native RFID</a> to 99.9% is what lets self-checkout read a basket in 30 seconds or less, and what makes an <a href="/platform/oms/" style="color: var(--brand-text);">Endless Aisle</a> or ship-from-store promise hold. BOPIS, BORIS and fiscal compliance in 40+ countries come with it.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          Which fashion and footwear brands use Teamwork Commerce?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Fashion and footwear retailers on the platform include ASICS, Lucchese, Lammle's Western Wear, Princesse Tam Tam and Comptoir des Cotonniers, City Beach, Havaianas, Texas Boot Company and Sandal Factory. It also serves luxury fashion brands including Acne Studios, Amiri, and The Row. It's localized in 40+ countries with native iOS POS, RFID, and integrated OMS.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

